  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q75-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equations simultaneously for $x$ and $y$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p5-q75-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}4^{x-y}&=8\\\\3^{x+2y}&=27\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$, $y=\\dfrac12$.\n\nEquate powers, then add the resulting linear equations.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^{2(x-y)}&=2^3\\\\3^{x+2y}&=3^3\\\\2x-2y&=3\\\\x+2y&=3\\end{align*}$$\nAdd the two linear equations.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x&=6\\\\x&=2\\\\2+2y&=3\\\\2y&=1\\\\y&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 74
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q76-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}5^{x-y}&=25^x\\\\4^{x+2y}&=\\frac12\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac12$, $y=-\\dfrac12$.\n\nEquate powers to obtain $y=-x$, then substitute into the other linear equation.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5^{x-y}&=5^{2x}\\\\x-y&=2x\\\\y&=-x\\\\2^{2(x+2y)}&=2^{-1}\\\\2x+4y&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $y=-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+4(-x)&=-1\\\\-2x&=-1\\\\x&=\\frac12\\\\y&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 74
      }
    ]
  },
